        "key_terms": ["process", "sunlight", "water", "carbon dioxide", "food", "chlorophyll", "oxygen"],
        "source_span": "Plants make their own food using sunlight. This process is called photosynthesis. A plant uses sunlight, water, and a gas from the air called carbon dioxide to make food. This happens mostly inside the leaves of the plant. Inside each leaf cell there is a green substance called chlorophyll, and chlorophyll is what captures the light energy from the sun. The plant's roots take in water from the soil, and the water travels up through the plant to reach the leaves. During photosynthesis, the plant also releases a gas called oxygen into the air, which people and animals need to breathe. Photosynthesis is how a plant grows and stays alive."
